{
  "_comment": "MAGIC v3 (design doc v3; designer session 2026-08-28). Every spell has a 'level' 1-5; its COST IS COMPUTED (level x 2 + 1 = 3/5/7/9/11 SP) — never add a 'cost'. WHO CASTS: 'classes' (ids from classes.json), gated by character level (spell level 1 at char 1-3, 2 at 4-7, 3 at 8-11, 4 at 12-15, 5 at 16-20). Wizards keep a SPELLBOOK from level 1 (classes.json 'spellbook'): they start with a kit, STUDY one common spell at set levels, and copy scrolls in. Priests know every common prayer; 'rare' prayers arrive as revelations (classes.json 'revelation_levels'). 'rare': true on an arcane spell = scroll-only lore (never studied — found on a scroll and copied in, or picked at the fork if it was already in the book). 'scroll': true = the engine makes a 'scroll_<id>' item (items.json 'scroll_values' ladder by level, 'rare_multiplier'); or {\"value\": N, \"tier\": T} to set them. Any ARCANE caster may read a scroll once in battle (I menu, 0 SP, up to max spell level + 1); only a spellbook may copy one. FIELDS: stat = ability whose modifier boosts the spell (int = arcane, wis = divine); type = damage | heal | buff | afflict | cure | raise; range/area in battle squares (area 1 = a 3x3 burst, 2 = 5x5, \"all\" = every foe on the field, range 0 = centered on the caster). Damage spells never miss: each target rolls a save (d20 + bonus vs DC 10 + spell level + caster's stat mod) — 'save' names the resisting ability; success = half damage; auto = true means no save at all. Damage bursts do NOT spare your friends (afflictions touch only foes). 'condition': {id, rounds} lands on targets that FAIL their save. AFFLICT = no damage, just the condition (save or suffer) — it honors 'area', and 'only_family': [\"undead\", ...] skips everyone else. 'double_vs': a monster family that takes double total damage (like Ancient weapons). 'drain': 0.5 = that fraction of damage dealt heals the caster. BUFFS: targets = self | ally (aim at one hero) | allies (the whole living party); fields hit, dmg, ac, saves, attacks (extra attacks per round), absorb (dice — a shield that drinks that much damage first), bonus_damage {dice, element} on every weapon hit, hidden (= the thief's Vanish), resist (elements, or \"all\" — half damage), immune_conditions; 'rounds' makes it timed (absent = the whole battle). Every buff wears its NAME in the combat math. HEAL: 'dice' to one ally at the crosshair, or targets 'allies' for the whole party; 'cures' also strips conditions. CURE: 'cures': [ids] or \"all\", optional dice. RAISE: a FALLEN ally rises with 'hp' (fraction of max). SCALE (caster-level growth, named 'caster level' in the log): {\"per_levels\": N, \"max\": M, and ONE of dice | flat | rounds | extra_targets | ac | area} — one step every N caster levels past the level the spell unlocked at (1/4/8/12/16), at most M steps. Magic Missile's extra_targets fires more darts at the nearest other foes. DAMAGE GUIDELINE (doc): ~2d6 per spell level. ALL numbers are CONTENT-FLAG proposals — rename, retune, add, and cut freely! VISUALS: optional \"fx\" — {\"kind\": bolt | beam | lightning | burst | sparkle | wisp, \"color\": hex, \"burst\": fire | frost | holy}. SOUND: fx \"sound\": fire | frost | lightning | light | arcane | sonic | cloud | web (heals and buffs are automatic); fire/frost/lightning/poison also decide which worn resistances guard a hero caught in the blast.",
